EXT. STALLED CABLE CAR - ALPINE GORGE - DAY

A red cable car hangs motionless a thousand feet above a frozen river. Wind rocks it gently.

INT. CABLE CAR - CONTINUOUS

HOLLIS BRANNIGAN (50s, park ranger, weathered face, steady hands) sits by the door with a thermos. He pours a cup and passes it along. INGRID SOLVANG (30s, climber, rope burns on her palms) takes it and smiles. She says nothing.

Beside her, TOMASZ KRAWIEC (40s, heavy coat, camera around his neck) photographs the gorge. His hands shake. KEIKO ARAI (20s, student, headphones around her neck) leans against the window, eyes closed. DARA NWOSU (30s, nurse, practical sneakers) checks a child's mitten, then pockets it.

HOLLIS
Power's out on the whole line. They'll winch us by dark.

TOMASZ
By dark? That's six hours.

HOLLIS
Closer to four.

He glances at the roof hatch. Nobody else notices.

DARA
You keep looking up.

HOLLIS
Habit.

She studies him. He drinks his coffee.

The radio on his belt crackles. Everyone looks at it.

RUFUS (V.O.)
(over radio)
Station to car four. Hollis, you read me?

Hollis thumbs the key.

HOLLIS
Loud and clear, Rufus. What's the word?

RUFUS (V.O.)
(over radio)
Don't let anybody open the hatch.

Silence. Tomasz lowers his camera. Keiko opens her eyes.

KEIKO
Why would he say that?

RUFUS (V.O.)
(over radio)
Because it isn't the wind, Hollis. Check the roof. Count the weight.

Hollis stands. The car dips, slow and heavy, toward the back. Ingrid grips the rail. Dara moves in front of Keiko. Tomasz backs away until he hits the glass.

Overhead, something shifts. A pause. Then three soft taps on the hatch, polite as a neighbor's.

TOMASZ
(whispering)
I count five of us.

DARA
There are five of us.

The taps come again. From underneath the floor.
